.TH CONKY-NEXTGEN 1 "October 2026" "conky-nextgen 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
conky-nextgen \- modular Conky theme framework, widget manager, and visual designer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B conky-nextgen
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIWIDGET\fR...]
.br
.B conky-nextgen
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B nextgen-designer
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBconky-nextgen\fR is an extensible desktop monitoring framework and modular widget suite built for \fBconky\fR(1). It integrates a high-performance Cairo-based Lua 5.4 graphics engine, asynchronous Bash backend data fetchers, responsive mouse event handling, and an integrated GTK3 visual designer.
.PP
Unlike monolithic Conky themes, \fBconky-nextgen\fR is designed like a set of \fBLEGO building blocks\fR. You can run the out-of-the-box widgets, reconfigure existing ones, or assemble entirely new widgets by snapping together modular drawing components and combining multiple Lua scripts.
.SH MODULAR ARCHITECTURE (THE LEGO SYSTEM)
The foundation of Conky NextGen is a declarative, component-driven Lua rendering pipeline.
.SS The Declarative Draw List
In any NextGen widget script (\fIwidget.lua\fR), visual components are appended as table objects into a global \fBdraw\fR list. The engine iterates over this list on every update cycle and renders each item using hardware-accelerated Cairo routines:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBdraw[#draw + 1] = {\fR
    \fBtype   = "background",\fR
    \fBx = 0, y = 0, w = 340, h = 200, radius = 12,\fR
\fB}\fR
\fBdraw[#draw + 1] = {\fR
    \fBtype   = "bar",\fR
    \fBconky_value = "${cpu cpu0}",\fR
    \fBx = 20, y = 60, w = 300, h = 10,\fR
\fB}\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Available modular building blocks include:
.TP
.B background
Rounded rectangle window container with solid, gradient, or bordered backgrounds.
.TP
.B clock
Customizable analog clock face with hour/minute/seconds hands, dial ticks, center cap, and optional numerals.
.TP
.B calendar
Clickable monthly calendar grid with navigable 4\(mu4 year and 3\(mu4 month selection popups, ISO week numbers, and date picking.
.TP
.B bar
Linear progress and metric bars with gradient color stops and background tracks.
.TP
.B graph
Real-time time-series telemetry graphs with custom grid lines, border styles, and color fills.
.TP
.B rings \fR/ \fBarc
Circular gauges and radial indicators with adjustable sweep angles and thickness.
.TP
.B text
Cairo text elements with font family, size, weight, alignment (left/center/right), and theme-driven colors.
.TP
.B lines
Horizontal and vertical decorative dividers or coordinate connection lines.
.TP
.B image \fR/ \fBsvg
Raster images (PNG/JPEG) with aspect scaling and mtime caching, or scalable vector graphics (SVG) rendered via \fBlibrsvg\fR.
.TP
.B spectrum
Dynamic multi-band audio spectrum bars connected to \fBcava\fR(1).
.TP
.B lyrics
Synchronized, scrolling song lyrics synchronized with active media players.
.SS Chaining Multiple Lua Scripts in lua_load
Conky allows loading \fBmultiple Lua scripts\fR simultaneously within a single configuration. In your \fIwidget.conf\fR, you can chain scripts in the \fIlua_load\fR property by separating their paths with spaces:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBlocal conf_dir = debug.getinfo(1, "S").source:match("@?(.*/)") or "./"\fR

\fBconky.config = {\fR
    \fB...\fR
    \fBlua_load = conf_dir .. 'base.lua ' .. conf_dir .. 'custom_hooks.lua',\fR
    \fBlua_draw_hook_pre = 'conky_core_main',\fR
\fB}\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
This architecture allows you to:
.IP \(bu 2
Reuse the core NextGen drawing engine while writing your own custom Lua logic, data scrapers, or Cairo renderers in a separate file.
.IP \(bu 2
Attach external Lua extensions without modifying the upstream widget code.
.IP \(bu 2
Override theme definitions or inject custom mouse handlers on the fly.
.SS Multi-View Navigation and Mouse Hooks
Widgets support multiple views (e.g. \fImain\fR, \fIview_1\fR, \fIview_2\fR) within the same window. Drawing elements can declare a \fBview\fR property to only show when that view is active. Mouse clicks can seamlessly flip between views (as demonstrated in \fIclock_cal\fR where clicking the clock toggles the full calendar view):
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBMOUSE_CLICK_LEFT = function() view_toggle("view_1") end\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH CUSTOMIZING WIDGETS & DESKTOP INTEGRATION (WIN+D FIX)
System widgets located under \fI/usr/share/conky-nextgen/\fR are read-only. To modify widget dimensions, screen alignments, or window behavior, copy the configuration to your user directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fB# Copy all templates into ~/.conky:\fR
\fBconky-nextgen init ~/.conky\fR

\fB# Or copy a single widget configuration:\fR
\fBcp /usr/share/conky-nextgen/clock_cal.conf ~/.conky/akarmi.conf\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
For a comprehensive manual of all window options, consult \fBman conky\fR(1). Note that in modern Conky 1.25+ (\fBconky-mng\fR), legacy options \fBown_window_argb_visual\fR (removed) and \fBown_window_transparent\fR (deprecated) are no longer used. ARGB support is always enabled, and background opacity is set natively via \fBown_window_color\fR with an alpha channel (e.g. \fB'#0000'\fR for complete transparency).
.PP
.SS Preventing Window Disappearing on "Show Desktop" (Super+D / Win+D)
In different desktop environments (MATE, GNOME, XFCE, KDE Plasma) or window managers, pressing the "Show Desktop" keyboard shortcut (\fBSuper+D\fR / \fBWin+D\fR) can minimize or hide Conky windows if the window type is not recognized by the compositor.
.PP
To fix this, adjust the \fBown_window_type\fR and \fBown_window_hints\fR properties in your user configuration:
.PP
.TP
.B 1. "normal" with below and sticky hints (Recommended for interactive mouse widgets in MATE and XFCE)
.RS
.nf
\fBown_window = true,\fR
\fBown_window_color = '#0000',\fR
\fBown_window_type = 'normal',\fR
\fBown_window_hints = 'undecorated,below,sticky,skip_taskbar,skip_pager',\fR
.fi
This mode allows full mouse event handling while preventing the widget from appearing in taskbars or pagers.
.RE
.TP
.B 2. "desktop" mode (Immune to Win+D in most compositors)
.RS
.nf
\fBown_window = true,\fR
\fBown_window_color = '#0000',\fR
\fBown_window_type = 'desktop',\fR
.fi
This attaches the window directly to the desktop root background.
.RE
.TP
.B 3. "dock" mode (Treated as an immutable desktop dock)
.RS
.nf
\fBown_window = true,\fR
\fBown_window_color = '#0000',\fR
\fBown_window_type = 'dock',\fR
\fBown_window_hints = 'undecorated,below,sticky,skip_taskbar,skip_pager',\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Once customized, launch your tailored configuration using:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBconky -c ~/.conky/akarmi.conf\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start \fR[\fIWIDGET\fR...]
Starts one or more widgets. If no widget names are supplied, starts the default suite (\fIclock_cal\fR, \fIcpu\fR, \fImem_swap\fR, \fIdisk_2_bars\fR, \fInetwork\fR, \fIweather\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fItop\fR, \fInow-playing\fR, \fIvnstat\fR, \fIgoogle\fR).
.TP
.B stop \fR[\fIWIDGET\fR...]
Stops specified widgets by name, or terminates all active Conky instances if no names are provided.
.TP
.B restart \fR[\fIWIDGET\fR...]
Restarts specified widgets or all active widgets.
.TP
.B status
Displays the execution status and process IDs (PIDs) of running NextGen widgets.
.TP
.B list
Lists all installed and user-available widget configurations along with their live state.
.TP
.B designer
Launches the \fBNextGen Designer\fR GTK3 visual editor.
.TP
.B fetch \fR[\fITARGET\fR] [\fICITY\fR]
Triggers background data collection scripts for weather, hardware metrics, network bandwidth, or media player metadata.
.TP
.B init \fR[\fIDIR\fR]
Initializes user configuration directory by copying default template configurations from \fI/usr/share/conky-nextgen/\fR into \fI~/.conky/\fR (or the specified target directory).
.SH AVAILABLE WIDGETS
.TP
.B clock_cal
Interactive analog clock and full monthly calendar. Left-clicking the clock toggles the calendar view. The calendar header features navigable 4\(mu4 year and 3\(mu4 month selection grids, ISO week numbers, and date pickers.
.TP
.B clock_cal_combi
Compact side-by-side analog clock and monthly calendar widget.
.TP
.B cpu
Real-time CPU monitoring showing multi-core usage bars, frequency graphs, and sensor temperatures.
.TP
.B mem_swap
Physical RAM and Swap memory utilization bars, percentage displays, and active allocations.
.TP
.B disk_2_bars
Storage monitoring with dual usage gauges for root (\fI/\fR) and user home (\fI/home\fR) partitions.
.TP
.B network
Network telemetry displaying dynamic upload/download speed graphs, active IP addresses, and link status.
.TP
.B weather
Comprehensive meteorological widget featuring Open-Meteo forecasts, WMO condition iconography, temperature gradients, hourly predictions, air quality indices, and weather alerts.
.TP
.B info
System dashboard showing OS release, Linux kernel version, host uptime, and package update counts.
.TP
.B top
Process monitor tracking highest consumers of CPU time and physical memory.
.TP
.B now-playing
Media player display supporting MPRIS2, Spotify, and Playerctl with synchronized track title, artist, progress, and album artwork.
.TP
.B vnstat
Bandwidth usage tracker utilizing \fBvnstat\fR(1) historical daily and monthly network logs.
.TP
.B google
Google account integration displaying upcoming Google Calendar appointments and Google Tasks.
.TP
.B visualizer
Audio spectrum bar visualizer synchronized with desktop audio streams via \fBcava\fR(1).
.TP
.B lyrics
Synchronized song lyric reader displaying time-stamped LRC lyrics.
.TP
.B nvidia
Hardware telemetry for systems equipped with dedicated NVIDIA graphics processors (utilization, VRAM, and thermal sensors).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays brief command-line syntax and usage summary.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Displays the installed version of conky-nextgen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/conky-nextgen/
System framework directory containing the shared Lua engine (\fIlua/\fR), icon sets (\fIicons/\fR), graphics (\fIimages/\fR), translations (\fIlanguage/\fR), backend scripts (\fIsh/\fR), and widget templates.
.TP
.I ~/.conky/
Default user configuration directory for customized \fI.conf\fR and \fI.lua\fR widget files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/conky-nextgen/
Persistent user preferences, geocoding language choices, and user-agent settings.
.TP
.I ${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/conky-nextgen/
Runtime in-memory temporary cache for fetched JSON metrics and weather forecasts.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CONKY_NEXTGEN_DIR
Overrides the system path to the NextGen framework (defaults to \fI/usr/share/conky-nextgen\fR).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Specifies the directory for ephemeral runtime data (defaults to \fI/run/user/$UID\fR or \fI/tmp\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start the flagship interactive clock and calendar:
.RS
.B conky-nextgen start clock_cal
.RE
.PP
Start CPU and memory monitors:
.RS
.B conky-nextgen start cpu mem_swap
.RE
.PP
Start the standard full desktop monitoring suite:
.RS
.B conky-nextgen start
.RE
.PP
Check active widget status:
.RS
.B conky-nextgen status
.RE
.PP
Stop all running Conky widgets:
.RS
.B conky-nextgen stop
.RE
.PP
Launch the graphical NextGen Designer:
.RS
.B conky-nextgen designer
.RE
